{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"symmetric-cubic-redstart","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Prove the ADR 0118 safety gate before this repository enables compact.snapshot_alpha. Use an independent clone pair, not only one working copy, to create divergent adaptive fold points, fetch/merge the tickets history, replay state, and run fsck/rebuild checks. Measure this repository's ticket-size distribution and benchmark candidate alpha values to recommend a project setting.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Independent two-clone reconvergence proof is checked in or reproducibly scripted and documents commands/results.\n- Divergent adaptive fold points converge after merge/replay/fsck without data loss or state divergence.\n- Calibration evidence recommends an alpha for this project with storage and replay-cost tradeoffs.\n- No rebar.toml enablement happens in this ticket.","id":"f670-8d14-15e7-4a04","parent_id":"da70-18a5-898d-47ea","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Prove snapshot_alpha reconvergence and calibrate"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788911818147171001,"uuid":"5452e77d-9b3a-40b9-a27e-c37470c28e67"}